  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88f6fa2b89436164b8e97b17d82dc9a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 12 - Indentation
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_indentation
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Indentation
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'You can use the <color=yellow>Tab key</color> on your keyboard to
    add indentation automatically.

    Indentation is the space at the beginning
    of a line that shows which code belongs together.


    Some parts of a program,
    like an <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D291FF>if</color></font> statement,
    use indentation to group multiple instructions into a single block.

    All
    code inside an <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D291FF>if</color></font> statement
    must use the same indentation level.


    Example:

    <indent=1em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#D291FF>if</color> condition:</font></indent>

    <indent=3em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#55FF55>mine</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font></indent>

    <indent=3em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#55FF55>move</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font></indent>


    If
    indentation is not correct, the program may not understand which instructions
    belong inside the <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D291FF>if</color></font>
    statement, which can cause errors or unexpected behavior.'
  isImageBig: 0
